{"kind":"request","text":"Stop merge artifacts claiming path dot, which makes that path a global mutex. Every merge states an artifact at dot superseding the previous one, so any merge flares anything anchored to any earlier merge: one branch counted forty live predecessors at that path. All four staleness incidents on 2026-08-09 were dot collisions rather than genuine behaviour drift. This needs no schema change and is independent of the describes-versus-reasoned-from ratification.","body":{"conditions":"Merge artifacts must name the paths the merge actually changed rather than the whole repository. Decide and state what the merged-head pointer becomes when a reader wants to ask 'what does main carry now' without a dot artifact to read, since that question is currently answered by the very artifact this request removes; if a separate merged-head record is the answer, it must not itself become a global mutex. Update AGENTS.md step 5 and SKILL.md discipline 8 to match, and say what existing dot artifacts mean afterwards - they are not retroactively wrong and should not be mass-superseded. Demonstrate on the real log that a merge touching one area no longer flares work anchored elsewhere, and that a merge touching a described area still does.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}